NAME

ulibFindFileSubDir - Finds the subdirectory a file is in


SYNOPSIS

long ulibFindFileSubDir(long Section, char *Name)
                             d0           a0


DESCRIPTION

This function returns the number of the subdirectory a particular file
catalogue entry is in, given the section number of the file, <Section>, and its
name, <Name>.

NOTE:  Once the file is located, the ulibFileSubDir() routine can be used to
       obtain the subdirectory's path, and thus the full path name of the file.


RETURNS

-1   - Physical file not found (i.e. file not currently online)
>= 0 - Number of subdirectory


SEE ALSO

ulibFileSubDir
